cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use these computations, please cite this repository."
title: "Open Problems Lab: reproducible computations on open problems in number theory and combinatorics"
type: software
version: "1.1.2"
abstract: >-
  Small, checkable computations on open problems in number theory and combinatorics,
  mostly from erdosproblems.com. Each note is a reproduction of published values, a finite
  computation past the published range, a negative result, or a proof of one finite
  statement checked by the Lean 4 kernel, with the scripts, outputs and an AI referee
  re-run report or the Lean files. The work was produced by AI agents and has not been
  reviewed by a human mathematician. Nothing here solves an open problem or claims a prize.
authors:
  - family-names: Lie
    given-names: Juwen
    orcid: "https://orcid.org/0009-0008-1384-7901"
keywords:
  - number theory
  - combinatorics
  - Erdos problems
  - reproducible computation
  - Lean 4
  - formal verification
  - computational mathematics
doi: 10.5281/zenodo.24338429
repository-code: "https://github.com/juw12/open-problems-lab"
date-released: 2026-11-25
license: MIT
